rue] [17592186311356 1110 #uuid "736246ce-6e99-51c1-804e-fe61834a2d55" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311357 1034 "$x=2$ only" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311357 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534808 true] [17592186311357 1111 #uuid "8dcf170c-0133-5a16-8d5e-3c13adb9ff7f" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311358 1034 "$x=1$  and $x=2$ only" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311358 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534808 true] [17592186311358 1111 #uuid "bf08b3cc-c355-587a-9fb1-db1f15dc0149" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311359 1034 "$x=0$  and $x=2$ only" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311359 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534808 true] [17592186311359 1111 #uuid "65c067d7-f046-5d57-8d8c-34c22b8730c3" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311360 1034 "$x=1$ only" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311360 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534808 true] [17592186311360 1111 #uuid "73f114d7-6f5c-551e-8bb9-063ca85bf34a" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311361 1034 "The function is differentiable at all points." 13194139534808 true] [17592186311361 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534808 true] [17592186311361 1111 #uuid "f25ef42a-3674-5ff0-9989-3a58615b83f2" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311362 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311363 13194139534808 true] [17592186311362 1089 "q-101998" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311362 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534808 true] [17592186311362 1100 "Which of the following functions is differentiable at the point $x=0?$" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311362 1113 #uuid "ea975bc3-faa7-5d1a-ad93-133065ece130" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311362 1145 "Notice that the function $q(x)$ is differentiable for all $x\\ne 1.$ Therefore, the correct answer is $q(x)={\\begin{aligned}x-1 & x<1 \\\\ x+1, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}.$\n\nAll other functions are not differentiable at $x=0.$\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not defined at $x=0$, so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $g(x)$ has a corner point at $x=0$, so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $p(x)$ has a vertical tangent at  $x=0$, so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $h(x)$ is not defined at $x=0$, so it is not differentiable there." 13194139534808 true] [17592186311363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311364 13194139534808 true] [17592186311363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311365 13194139534808 true] [17592186311363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311366 13194139534808 true] [17592186311363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311367 13194139534808 true] [17592186311363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311368 13194139534808 true] [17592186311363 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534808 true] [17592186311363 1041 "selection" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311363 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311364 13194139534808 true] [17592186311363 1110 #uuid "16f147b0-9ddc-539f-b672-71f768b20b62" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311364 1034 "q(x)={\\begin{aligned}x-1 & x<1 \\\\ x+1, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311364 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534808 true] [17592186311364 1111 #uuid "462d0bb6-ff7f-5d0e-bff0-1c60d80acbbe" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311365 1034 "g(x)=-|x|" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311365 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534808 true] [17592186311365 1111 #uuid "1fe2d17f-ff9a-5fe5-8348-82e9ecb1583c" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311366 1034 "h(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534808 true] [17592186311366 1111 #uuid "e0223612-a2eb-5def-9410-713fbfb11683" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311367 1034 "p(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534808 true] [17592186311367 1111 #uuid "6f452688-dfec-5200-bde2-7a963ffe7b49" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311368 1034 "f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311368 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534808 true] [17592186311368 1111 #uuid "ebeecb9f-e3db-510e-a4f1-5338a2743059" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311369 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311370 13194139534808 true] [17592186311369 1089 "q-47679" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311369 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534808 true] [17592186311369 1100 "Given that that a function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$, has a jump discontinuity at $x=2$, and  is differentiable at $x=3$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\n- It is differentiable at $x=1$\n- It  is **not** differentiable at $x=2$\n- It is continuous at $x=3$" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311369 1113 #uuid "ce79bb41-27b4-5b41-8558-5c87fd6419d0" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311369 1145 "- Statement I is false. Continuity does not imply differentiability. For example, the function $y=|x-1|$ is continuous but it's not differentiable at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true.  A function that is discontinuous at a point can't be differentiable at this point (because differentiability implies continuity).\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, differentiability implies continuity." 13194139534808 true] [17592186311370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311371 13194139534808 true] [17592186311370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311372 13194139534808 true] [17592186311370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311373 13194139534808 true] [17592186311370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311374 13194139534808 true] [17592186311370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311375 13194139534808 true] [17592186311370 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534808 true] [17592186311370 1041 "selection" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311370 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311373 13194139534808 true] [17592186311370 1110 #uuid "4a40f4f1-0f18-549a-bebf-abfe7f0c4dca" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311371 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534808 true] [17592186311371 1111 #uuid "d0dcf4d5-9f47-5ef3-8cca-8d6e4015fb5a" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311372 1034 "I only" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534808 true] [17592186311372 1111 #uuid "1aa03c7e-e846-57c8-ab0c-d3f972808f73" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311373 1034 "II and  III only" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534808 true] [17592186311373 1111 #uuid "b215d962-5791-5437-98a0-e524d0193852" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311374 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311374 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534808 true] [17592186311374 1111 #uuid "67b4f277-4b85-5a80-a9d1-40654b33c52b" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311375 1034 "II only" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311375 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534808 true] [17592186311375 1111 #uuid "dd83a898-96f9-523f-948e-e7db6ba6c270" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311376 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311377 13194139534808 true] [17592186311376 1089 "q-47686" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311376 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534808 true] [17592186311376 1100 "Which of the following functions is not differentiable over the interval $(-1,1)$ due to the existence of a vertical asymptote at a point in this interval?" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311376 1113 #uuid "509c565e-90e4-5255-a4cc-bb56af4023be" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311376 1145 "The function $y=g(x)$ has a vertical asymptote at $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and is  therefore not differentiable at $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ So $y=g(x)$ is the correct answer.\n\nThe other graphs do not have a a vertical asymptote inside the interval $(-1,1).$\n\n- The function $y=p(x)$ has a corner point at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and is therefore not differentiable at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The function $y=h(x)$ has a vertical tangent at $x=0$ and is therefore not differentiable at $x=0.$\n\n- The function $y=q(x)$ is smooth and continuous over the entire interval $x\\in (-1,1)$ and is therefore differentiable at every point in the interval.\n\n- The function $y=f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and is therefore not differentiable at $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311378 13194139534808 true] [17592186311377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311379 13194139534808 true] [17592186311377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311380 13194139534808 true] [17592186311377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311381 13194139534808 true] [17592186311377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311382 13194139534808 true] [17592186311377 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534808 true] [17592186311377 1041 "selection" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311377 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311380 13194139534808 true] [17592186311377 1110 #uuid "12203f6f-7440-5b0c-9932-ecf631576a1e" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311378 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041401/assets/a8b5f35bec07979fc1e0d1eb4de3e6ad369bbce48ec4e1943380b9bac2e9feee.png" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534808 true] [17592186311378 1111 #uuid "e0a642e4-3fc5-5ed1-8b02-6ffeba569d3f" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311379 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041401/assets/3ec213a7183bd1a9ed039d185361581b4a687462a8bfd0e5f885090bf53bf09f.png" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534808 true] [17592186311379 1111 #uuid "d240a1c3-78f2-5554-b048-4e7efcdd19ea" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311380 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041401/assets/2733ec295867c20225f4b5d75f5cbe4bfbc91d9b8f3739520bcf4ce75c4d185c.png" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534808 true] [17592186311380 1111 #uuid "728ca005-3873-541b-a9e1-018363568381" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311381 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041401/assets/1f9ccdd0ab4829b8f5fe53660c8d7a48dd5f85b90f979bc7d927e4a141d2e6c2.png" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311381 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534808 true] [17592186311381 1111 #uuid "f8676dba-6d46-56c1-afa9-ab19df53e26a" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311382 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041401/assets/6d8c3bcf0d95b358b601f55746b256d1edf936c88e0dc4bd6c119fdb45327150.png" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534808 true] [17592186311382 1111 #uuid "1d723d76-f3af-5954-b786-cdf27bdced07" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311383 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311384 13194139534808 true] [17592186311383 1089 "q-51072" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311383 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534808 true] [17592186311383 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-x+4, & x<1 \\\\ 0, & x=1 \\\\ x+2, & x>1\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\n- It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n- It is differentiable on the interval $(-2,2)$\n- It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311383 1113 #uuid "ba6055fe-aa65-5082-af20-e73dcea7d739" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311383 1145 "- Statement I is false and statement III is true. Indeed,  let's investigate the continuity of $f(x).$ It is continuous everywhere except, possibly, $x=1.$ At this point, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}(-x+4)=-1+4=3 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(x+2)=1+2=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)\\ne f(1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$ (it has a removable discontinuity there). Hence, it is also not differentiable at this point.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=1,$ it is not differentiable on any interval containing this point. Consequently, it is not differentiable on $(-2,2).$" 13194139534808 true] [17592186311384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311385 13194139534808 true] [17592186311384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311386 13194139534808 true] [17592186311384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311387 13194139534808 true] [17592186311384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311388 